@startuml Timeloop Execution Flow

!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Timeloop Mapper - Execution Flow Sequence

actor User
participant "Mapper\nApplication" as Mapper
participant "Config\nParser" as Config
participant "Search\nAlgorithm" as Search
participant "MapSpace" as MapSpace
participant "Engine" as Engine
participant "Nest\nAnalysis" as Analysis
participant "Output\nGenerator" as Output

== Initialization ==

User -> Mapper: Run with config files\n(arch, problem, mapper)
activate Mapper

Mapper -> Config: Parse configuration
activate Config
Config -> Config: Parse architecture spec
Config -> Config: Parse workload spec
Config -> Config: Parse mapper config
Config -> Config: Parse constraints
Config --> Mapper: Return parsed specs
deactivate Config

Mapper -> Engine: Initialize engine\nwith arch specs
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine: Build topology\n(levels, buffers, networks)
Engine --> Mapper: Ready
deactivate Engine

Mapper -> MapSpace: Initialize mapspace\nwith constraints
activate MapSpace
MapSpace -> MapSpace: Compute mapspace size
MapSpace -> MapSpace: Initialize iterators
MapSpace --> Mapper: Ready
deactivate MapSpace

== Multi-threaded Search ==

Mapper -> Mapper: Create N threads

loop For each thread
  Mapper -> Search: Spawn search thread
  activate Search
  
  loop Until termination condition
    Search -> MapSpace: Get next mapping
    activate MapSpace
    MapSpace -> MapSpace: Generate candidate\nmapping
    MapSpace --> Search: Return mapping
    deactivate MapSpace
    
    Search -> Engine: Evaluate mapping
    activate Engine
    
    Engine -> Analysis: Analyze loop nest
    activate Analysis
    
    Analysis -> Analysis: Compute tiling
    Analysis -> Analysis: Temporal analysis
    Analysis -> Analysis: Spatial analysis
    Analysis -> Analysis: Compute data movement
    Analysis -> Analysis: Compute energy
    Analysis -> Analysis: Compute cycles
    
    Analysis --> Engine: Return metrics
    deactivate Analysis
    
    alt Mapping is valid
      Engine --> Search: Return stats\n(energy, cycles, etc.)
      
      Search -> Search: Compare with\nbest mapping
      
      alt Better than best
        Search -> Search: Update best mapping
        Search -> Search: Log new optimum
      else Not better
        Search -> Search: Increment\nsuboptimal counter
      end
      
    else Mapping is invalid
      Engine --> Search: Return failure
      Search -> Search: Increment\ntimeout counter
    end
    
    deactivate Engine
    
    alt Termination condition met
      Search -> Search: Exit loop
    end
  end
  
  Search -> Mapper: Return thread results\n(best mapping, stats)
  deactivate Search
end

== Result Collection ==

Mapper -> Mapper: Collect results\nfrom all threads
Mapper -> Mapper: Select global\nbest mapping

Mapper -> Engine: Final evaluation\nof best mapping
activate Engine
Engine -> Analysis: Detailed analysis
activate Analysis
Analysis --> Engine: Complete stats
deactivate Analysis
Engine --> Mapper: Final results
deactivate Engine

== Output Generation ==

Mapper -> Output: Generate outputs
activate Output

Output -> Output: Generate mapping\ndescription (YAML, C++)
Output -> Output: Generate statistics\n(energy, cycles, accesses)
Output -> Output: Generate Tensella\ncode (optional)
Output -> Output: Generate visualization\n(optional)

Output --> Mapper: Output strings
deactivate Output

Mapper --> User: Write output files
deactivate Mapper

User -> User: Review results

note right of Search
  **Termination Conditions:**
  - timeout: N consecutive invalid mappings
  - victory_condition: M consecutive suboptimal mappings
  - search_size: Total valid mappings evaluated
  
  **Search Algorithms:**
  - Exhaustive
  - Random / Random Pruned
  - Linear Pruned
  - Hybrid (default)
end note

note right of Engine
  **Evaluation Metrics:**
  - Energy consumption
  - Execution cycles
  - Memory accesses
  - Network transfers
  - Hardware utilization
  - Area (optional)
end note

note left of Analysis
  **Analysis Steps:**
  1. Tiling calculation
  2. Temporal reuse analysis
  3. Spatial distribution
  4. Data movement quantification
  5. Energy/performance modeling
  6. ISL polyhedral analysis (optional)
  7. Sparse optimization (optional)
end note

@enduml
